   "gap": "Barwise's Cut-Elimination Theorem 4.14 (Gentzen): any sequent that has a derivation with the cut rule has one without it, i.e. G+ and G have the same derivable sequents. It is stated at w02-p02-005 lines 1066-1072 but recorded only as Barwise's claim (line 1075: 'Neither route is carried out for G'). The source gives its proof route on printed p. 40: prove completeness of the cut-free system G directly, expanding the proof of the propositional part 4.12 to G's equality axioms, equality rule and four quantifier rules. Owed: that complete route written out with its exact hypotheses (G's sequents, the eigenvariable condition on (|-forall) and (exists|-), the equality axioms and rule), i.e. a written proof that every sequent true in all structures is derivable in G, from which 4.14 follows with complete steps. Separately, the owned-file results that make Barwise's recursion 'by induction on length' define a function and that justify his truth-table test are written with complete annex proofs but are route pending.",
